nora (docs): Small UX snag: the Java quickstart sample app prints a full stack trace that includes a placeholder API key example. New users copy it into their repos and then hit 401s.

nora (docs): snippet from quickstarts/java/README.md: ```java
// BAD - prints stack with placeholder token and suggests putting key in source
try {
  RedwoodClient client = new RedwoodClient("sk-placeholder-123");
  var out = client.generate(request);
} catch (Exception e) {
  e.printStackTrace(); // includes the literal token in logs in some setups
}
```

leo (devex): Yikes. We should remove the hardcoded token, avoid printing full stack traces in examples, and show use of System.getenv / config file + recommend structured logging with redaction.

emma (sdk): I'll open a small PR to swap the snippet. Proposed replacement: ```java
// GOOD - read key from env + redact on error
RedwoodClient client = new RedwoodClient(System.getenv("REDWOOD_API_KEY"));
try {
  var out = client.generate(request);
} catch (Exception e) {
  logger.error("Generation failed: {}", e.getMessage()); // don't log full stack or secrets
  throw e;
}
```

emma (sdk): Also adding a note in the README about using a secret manager for production and how to rotate keys without redeploys.

ci-bot: docs-lint: failure -> quickstarts/java/README.md line 18: detected literal token pattern sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{6,}. See https://ci.internal/jobs/9022

leo (devex): Can we add a linter rule to scan code fences for e.printStackTrace or logging methods that interpolate exceptions including toString()? Those often reveal sensitive data.

emma (sdk): Good call. I'll add a docs-validator check to flag common patterns: e.printStackTrace(), Exception#toString in logs, and sk- token regex. Adding a unit test in sdk repo and linking PR.

nora (docs): Opening issue #1302 to track; will add the PR link to the issue once it's up. Small change but prevents a lot of "where did my key go" troubleshooting. :lock:
